  "title": "CHAPTER 11: PLANT KINGDOM (DETAILED VERSION)",
  "order": 11,
  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "67jzwua",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Introduction to Plant Kingdom"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The Plant Kingdom is broadly classified into Thallophyta, Bryophyta, Pteridophyta, Gymnosperms, and Angiosperms.",
        "Angiosperms represent flowering plants and are subdivided into Monocotyledons and Dicotyledons based on seed structure.",
        "Vascular tissues (xylem and phloem) differentiate lower non-vascular plants (Thallophyta, Bryophyta) from higher vascular plants.",
        "Plant life cycles feature Alternation of Generations between haploid gametophyte and diploid sporophyte stages.",
        "Evolutionary trends show advancement from aquatic, thalloid forms to terrestrial, seed-bearing vascular plants."
      ],
      "id": "1ge7du8"
    },
    {
      "type": "statStrip",
      "stats": [
        {
          "label": "Major Divisions",
          "value": "5 Groups",
          "icon": "book"
        },
