      "id": "7f0jct5"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "vza5ot4",
      "content": "Kingdom Plantae includes multicellular, eukaryotic, autotrophic organisms. They possess chlorophyll and perform photosynthesis. Plant classification is mainly based on body differentiation, presence of vascular tissues, and seed formation."
    },
    {
      "id": "uk412ye",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "2. Basis of Classification in Plants"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ufhb9sy",
      "content": "• Presence or absence of vascular tissues (xylem and phloem)."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "hxp3j6j",
      "content": "• Presence or absence of seeds."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "n40qzot",
      "content": "• Nature of seeds (naked or enclosed)."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "gstf7op",
      "content": "• Differentiation of plant body."
    },
    {
      "id": "y1sdzuh",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "3. Major Divisions of Plant Kingdom"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "qzsx5pb",
      "content": "The Plant Kingdom is divided into Thallophyta, Bryophyta, Pteridophyta, Gymnosperms and Angiosperms. "
