      "id": "p3rkl8u",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "18. Quick Exam Facts (RRB Focus)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "3512z3i",
      "content": "1. Bryophytes are amphibians of plant kingdom."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "orrpjhq",
      "content": "2. Pteridophytes are first vascular plants."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "3781dxs",
      "content": "3. Gymnosperms have naked seeds."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "jsbqxi8",
      "content": "4. Angiosperms are flowering plants."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "si7dw9n",
      "content": "5. Monocot – parallel venation."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "zpk8otu",
      "content": "6. Dicot – tap root system."
    }
